::kind(api)

::meta(crate: sisho-board-core, dependencies: (sisho-board-sdk), dependents: (sisho-board))

=[sisho-board-core]

The operating dashboard and board for the Tomet ecosystem (`sisho-board`).

Two-tier design:

- @strong[Board]: Status of tools, extensions (with explicit user trust via `sisho`),

extension board panes (`--sisho-board-pane`), integrity check outcomes, and broken links.

- @strong[Counter]: Action prompt bar to run check, fix, check-links, manage extension trust, or open desk.

==[Module config]

Portable UI board configuration (`$SISHO_CONFIG_DIR/board.json` or `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sisho/board/board.json`).

`BoardConfig` stores only portable UI preferences (such as hidden extension panes)
with zero binary paths and zero trust state. Extension execution trust is owned
exclusively by `sisho` (`~/.local/share/sisho/trust.json`).

===[Structs]

====[struct BoardConfig]

Portable UI customization for `sisho-board` (`board.json`).

===[Functions]

====[fn default_config_path]

Resolve the default path to `board.json`:

- `$SISHO_CONFIG_DIR/board.json` if `SISHO_CONFIG_DIR` is set and non-empty
- otherwise `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sisho/board/board.json`
- otherwise `$HOME/.config/sisho/board/board.json`

Matches `sisho_sdk::config_dir("board")`.

====[fn resolve_config_path_with]

Resolve the path to `board.json` using a custom environment variable lookup function.

Matches `sisho_sdk::config_dir("board")`.

===[Constants]

====[const CURRENT_BOARD_CONFIG_SCHEMA_VERSION]

Current schema version for `board.json`.

==[Module editor]

Editor resolution for opening broken link files from `sisho-board`.

===[Functions]

====[fn resolve_editor]

Resolve an editor command to open `file` at `line`.

Precedence chain:
1. `$SISHO_EDITOR` (handles `{file}`, `{line}`, `{col}` templates, allowed extension words, or commands)
2. `$VISUAL` (Unix full-screen editor: nvim, vim, hx, etc.)
3. `$EDITOR` (Unix standard editor)
4. `sisho-desk` (if installed, active, and \[`TrustState::Allowed`\])
5. `nano` (system fallback)

====[fn resolve_editor_with_lookup]

==[Module extension]

Extension discovery and protocol querying (`--sisho-extension-info` and `--sisho-board-pane`).

Security boundary: \[`scan`\] and \[`scan_in`\] only inspect directory entries
and file permissions on `PATH`; they never execute any discovered program.
\[`query_info`\] and \[`query_board_pane`\] must only be called for extensions
whose \[`TrustState`\] is \[`TrustState::Allowed`\].

===[Functions]

====[fn is_valid_word]

True if `word` is a valid extension name (`[a-z0-9-]+`, not starting with `-`).

====[fn discover]

Discover extensions by delegating to `<sisho_program> --list --json`, falling
back safely to \[`scan`\] with all extensions marked \[`TrustState::Untrusted`\]
if `sisho` is missing or older.

====[fn scan]

Scan `PATH` for `sisho-<word>` extension executables (excluding `sisho-board` itself).

Never executes any discovered binary. All returned items start with
\[`TrustState::Untrusted`\].

====[fn scan_in]

Scan specific directories for `sisho-<word>` extension executables.

====[fn extension_dir_envs]

Compute `SISHO_CONFIG_DIR` and `SISHO_DATA_DIR` environment variable pairs for `word`.

Resolves `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sisho/<word>` (fallback `$HOME/.config/sisho/<word>`)
and `$XDG_DATA_HOME/sisho/<word>` (fallback `$HOME/.local/share/sisho/<word>`),
ignoring `sisho-board`'s own `SISHO_CONFIG_DIR` and `SISHO_DATA_DIR` so board's
directories never leak into queried extensions.

====[fn extension_dir_envs_with]

Compute `SISHO_CONFIG_DIR` and `SISHO_DATA_DIR` for `word` using a custom env lookup.

====[fn query_info]

Query an allowed extension executable for its `--sisho-extension-info` metadata.

====[fn query_board_pane]

Query an allowed extension executable for its `--sisho-board-pane <dir>` data.

==[Module health]

Vault and repository Readiness & Health (`%`) measurement engine.

Evaluates six deterministic pillars across a Tomet vault or repository:
1. @strong[Tomet Coverage]: `.tmt` source files + generated `.md` artifacts vs unmigrated `.md` files.
2. @strong[`::id` Declaration]: share of eligible `.tmt` documents declaring `::id(...)`.
3. @strong[`::kind` & Blueprint Coverage]: share of eligible `.tmt` documents declaring `::kind(...)` or `::blueprint(...)`, enriched with `tomet stats --json`.
4. @strong[Link Health]: unbroken links vs total checked links from `tomet check-links --json`.
5. @strong[Writ & Catasto Governance]: presence of `.writ.tmt`, guarded `@rule(...)` blocks, and `catasto.lock` consistency.
6. @strong[Cleanliness & Freshness]: absence of `@draft` markers and validation errors/warnings, plus documentation vs code freshness.

===[Structs]

====[struct PillarMetric]

Score and diagnostic detail for one readiness pillar.

====[struct HealthReport]

Complete Readiness & Health report for a vault or repository.

===[Functions]

====[fn status_for_percent]

Status threshold for a percentage (`100` -> `Pass`, `70..=99` -> `Warn`, `<70` -> `Fail`).

====[fn analyze]

Analyze the vault/repository at `dir`, invoking `tomet stats --json` if `tomet` is available.

====[fn analyze_with_stats]

Analyze the vault/repository at `dir` with an optional pre-fetched `tomet stats --json` payload.

==[Module links]

The link check as the board shows it: what `tomet check-links --json`
reports about the links of a vault that point at nothing.

===[Structs]

====[struct Position]

A line and a column, both counted from 1.

====[struct BrokenLink]

A link whose target does not exist.

====[struct Unreadable]

A document that could not be looked at.

====[struct Report]

What a run found.

===[Functions]

====[fn check]

Check the links under `dir` by running `tomet check-links --json`.

==[Module model]

State model and background worker coordination for `sisho-board`.

===[Structs]

====[struct ExtensionItem]

An extension discovered on `PATH` and presented on the Board.

====[struct PendingTrustPrompt]

Pending confirmation prompt for changing an extension's trust state via `sisho`.

====[struct ToolStatus]

Status of a core ecosystem tool (`tomet`, `twrit`, `catasto`).

====[struct ExtensionPaneItemRef]

Reference to a single item inside an allowed extension's \[`BoardPane`\].

====[struct Model]

The state of the board and counter.

===[Enums]

====[enum StepSlot]

A slot representing a check or fix step in progress or completed.

====[enum FocusedPane]

The currently focused pane on the Board.

====[enum PreviewSource]

Which pane provides the content currently shown in the Output Preview pane.

====[enum WorkerMessage]

